  "transform": "erase the source segment; keep background unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square, 10-20 rows/cols [observed: always 16x16]
  colors:
    background: single color filling the grid
    foreground: one non-bg color [observed: bg=7, fg=2]
  segment:
    shape: contiguous 1-pixel-wide run on a single anti-diagonal (r+c = D)
    length: 1-7 pixels (must allow output length L+1 to fit in grid)
    orientation: each pixel at (D-c, c) for consecutive columns c_start..c_start+L-1
  anti_diagonal_sum: any D such that both input and output segments fit in grid
  output_rule: |
    Erase input segment of length L at cols [c_start, c_start+L-1].
    Draw new segment of length L+1 at cols [c_start+L, c_start+2L]
    on the same anti-diagonal. Output is otherwise all background.
  fit_constraint: |
    For input: 0 <= c_start, c_start+L-1 <= N-1, 0 <= D-c_start-L+1, D-c_start <= N-1.
    For output: 0 <= c_start+L, c_start+2L <= N-1, 0 <= D-c_start-2L, D-c_start-L <= N-1.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick grid size N (square, 10-20).
    - Pick bg and fg colors (fg != bg).
    - Pick output segment length L_out in [2, floor(N/2)].
    - Set input length L_in = L_out - 1.
    - Enumerate all valid (D, c_in) pairs where both input (cols c_in..c_in+L_in-1) and output (cols c_in+L_in..c_in+L_in+L_out-1) segments fit in the NxN grid on anti-diagonal D. Pick one uniformly.
    - Fill NxN grid with bg, place fg at input segment positions (D-c, c) for c in [c_in, c_in+L_in-1].
```
